$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of this anilide-alcohol (1.43g, 4.48 mmol) in DMSO (15 mL)
was added IBX (2.51 g, 8.95 mmol) and the reaction mixture was stirred at
room temperature for 12 h. The reaction mixture was quenched upon
addition of 5% aqueous NaHCO3 (50 mL) and diluted with EtOAc (50 mL). The
layers were separated and the organic layer was washed with 5% aqueous
NaHCO3 (2 x 20 mL), water (2 x 20 mL) and brine (30 mL) and then dired
(Na2SO4) and concentrated. Pure aldehyde-anilide (1.48 g, 100% yield).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Iodine(V) Reagents in Organic Synthesis. Part 2. Access to Complex
Molecular Architectures via Dess-Martin Periodinane-Generated
o-Imidoquinones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
