$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-(4-(Diphenylamino)phenyl)propiolaldehyde (3a). To a solution of
compound 2a (1.76 g, 5.87 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (0.1 M, 60 mL) was added the
Dess-Martin periodinane (DMP) (6.47 g, 14.2 mmol) in one portion. The
solution was stirred at room temperature for 1 h. Then the mixture was
diluted with water and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 × 50 mL). The combined
organic layers were washed with water and brine and dried with anhydrous
Na2SO4. The solvent was evaporated, and the remaining crude product was
purified by column chromatography using silica gel and CH2Cl2 as the
eluent gave pure compound 3a as dark yellow oil (1.75 g, yield 100%).
3-(4-(Diphenylamino)phenyl)propiolaldehyde (3a), yield 1.75 g, 100% 1H
NMR (400 Hz, acetone-d6, ppm): δ 9.41 (s, 1H), 7.58-7.36 (m, 6H),
7.34-7.16 (m, 6H), 7.03 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H). GCT/TOF HRMS-EI (m/z): [M]+
calcd. for C21H15NO, 297.1154; found, 297.1160.
