$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Dess-Martin reagent (0.3 M in DCM, 607 μL, 0.18 mmol) was added to a
solution of 20 (555 mg, 0.17 mmol) in DCM (1 mL). After 1 h at room
temperature, the reaction was quenched with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (2
mL) and 300 mg solid Na2S2O3·5H2O. The organic phase was dried (MgSO4),
filtered, and concentrated at reduced pressure to afford 21 as an oil
which was carried on directly. Amber oil, yield 55 mg, 100%. 1H NMR (400
MHz, chloroform-d) δ 9.70 (dd, J = 2.05, 14.94 Hz, 1H), 7.21-7.28 (m,
4H), 7.12-7.19 (m, 1H), 7.04-7.09 (m, 1H), 6.90 (d, J = 7.62 Hz, 1H),
2.43-2.50 (m, 1H), 2.31-2.40 (m, 1H), 1.38-1.52 (m, 9H). MS (ES+) m/z:
261.3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Dess-Martin oxidation (stage 1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery and optimization of a novel spiropyrrolidine inhibitor of
β-secretase (BACE1) through fragment-based drug design
