$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (Z)-Non-3-enal (3b). To a solution of (Z)-non-3-enol (2b, 0.429 g, 3.02
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (30 mL) under argon was added at 0°C the DMP (1.66 g,
3.91 mmol). After 5 min, the reaction mixture was allowed to warm up to
r.t. and stirred for 1 h, then cooled down to -15°C and diluted with
pentane (30 mL). The white suspension was quickly filtered through a pad
of silica gel pre-impregnated with Et2O-pentane (1:4) and cooled between
-40°C and -50°C. The silica was rinsed with cold Et2O-pentane (100 mL,
1:4). The clear solution was concentrated and dried by azeotropic
distillation of benzene under vacuum. The (Z)-non-3-enal (3b) was
obtained. Colorless oil, yield 0.42 g, 98%. Rf = 0.64 (Et2O-pentane,
1:1). IR (film): 2924, 1728, 1470 cm-1. 1H NMR: δ = 9.64 (t, 1 H, J = 2.0
Hz, CHO), 5.68 (dtt, 1 H, J = 10.8, 7.3, 1.5 Hz, CH2CH2CH), 5.51 (dtt, 1
H, J = 10.8, 7.3, 1.7 Hz, CHCH2CHO), 3.18-3.14 (br ddd, 2 H, J = 7.3,
2.0, 1.5 Hz, CH2CHO), 2.06-1.97 (br quint, 2 H, J = 7.4 Hz, CH2CH2CH),
1.39-1.22 (m, 6 H, CH3(CH2)3), 0.86 (t, 3 H, J = 6.9 Hz, CH3). 13C NMR: δ
= 199.7 (CHO), 135.4 (CH2CH2CH), 118.0 (CHCH2CHO), 42.5 (CH2CHO), 31.4
(CH2CH2CH), 29.0, 27.6, 22.5 (3 CH2), 14.0 (CH3).
