$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of Dess-Martin periodinane (561 mg, 1.32 mmol) in CH2Cl2
(13 mL, 0.05 M) at 25 °C was added NaHCO3 (830 mg, 9.9 mmol) and allylic
alcohol 9c (439 mg, 0.66 mmol). The reaction was stirred for 2 h at 25
°C, at which point it was quenched with pH 7 phosphate buffer. The
mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2 for three times and the combined
organic fractions were dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The
residue was purified by column chromatography (SiO2; ethyl
acetate:hexanes, 1:8 to 1:4) to provide Fragment A (425 mg, 0.64 mmol) as
a colorless oil in 97% yield. Yield (425 mg, 0.64 mmol, 97%). 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.33 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.72-7.68 (m, 4H), 7.46-7.36 (m,
6H), 6.68 (d, J = 16.0 Hz, 1H), 6.35 (dt, J = 16.7, 10.8 Hz, 1H), 5.98
(dd, J = 16.0, 6.6 Hz, 1H), 5.90 (d, J = 10.8 Hz, 1H), 5.27-5.22 (m, 1H),
5.01 (s, 1H), 4.13-4.07 (m, 1H), 3.79-3.75 (m, 1H), 3.52-3.45 (m, 1H),
2.48 (dd, J = 14.0, 9.6 Hz, 1H), 2.10 (dd, J = 14.0, 4.8 Hz, 1H), 1.98
(s, 3H), 1.62-1.53 (m, 1H), 1.48-1.42 (m, 1H), 1.28 (s, 3H), 1.26 (s,
3H), 1.21 (s, H), 1.19 (s, 3H), 1.17 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 3H), 1.04 (s, 9H).
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 204.5, 193.4, 170.1, 159.6, 137.2, 136.0,
136.0, 134.1, 133.7, 131.6, 130.9, 130.1, 129.9, 128.9, 127.9, 127.8,
122.5, 107.9, 79.1, 78.5, 77.0, 69.9, 50.3, 39.8, 38.7, 27.7, 27.3, 27.0,
24.1, 24.1, 20.5, 19.6, 17.1. FTIR (neat): ν 3074, 3052, 2976, 2927,
2865, 2740, 2148, 2006, 1748, 1712, 1694, 1472, 1432, 1378, 1227, 1089,
1054, 996, 911, 742, 698 cm-1. HRMS (ESI) Calcd. for C39H52O7SiNa
[M+Na]+: 683.3375, Found: 683.3373. [α]26 D: + 32.0° (c = 1.00, CHCl3).
TLC (SiO2): Rf = 0.36 (ethyl acetate:hexanes, 1:4).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM buffered soln. in 2nd stage/phosphate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Total synthesis of bryostatin 7 via C-C bond-forming hydrogenation
