$DATUM 5,6,13,14-Tetradehydro-7,8,9,10,11,12-hexahydrobenzo[12]annulene-7,9-dione
(32). A solution of β-hydroxyketone 31 (0.259 g, 1.09 mmol) in dry
dichloromethane (5 mL) was added to a stirred suspension of the
Dess-Martin periodinane (0.620 g, 1.46 mmol) in dry dichloromethane (30
mL). After 3 h the reaction mixture was diluted with ether (60 mL),
stirred for 30 min, and washed with saturated aqueous sodium bicarbonate
solution (2 x 50 mL) and brine (100 mL). Aqueous phases were
back-extracted with ether (50 mL). Combined organic phases were dried
over magnesium sulphate, filtered, evaporated under reduced pressure, and
the solid residue was purified by column chromatography (20% ethyl
acetate in hexanes, Rf = 0.30) to yield 0.249g (1.06 mmol, 97%) of 32 as
colourless crystalline solid. M.p. 98-990C; FW calc. for
C16H12O2:236.0837, EI-HRMS found: 236.0837, EI-MS m/z: 236(20) [M+],
221(1), 208(14), 194(5), 179(42), 165(100), 152(48), 138(35), 126(4),
115(2), 111(2); 1H-NMR (300 MHz): 1.94 (qin, J = 6.3 Hz, 2H), 2.69 (t, J
= 6.3 Hz, 2H), 3.17 (t, J = 6 Hz, 2H), 3.74 (s, 2H), 7.23-7.32 (m, 1H),
7.35-7.41 (m, 2H), 7.53 (m, 1H); 13C-NMR (75 MHz): 18.25, 19.88, 42.45,
59.60, 80.50, 89.58, 92.63, 94.94, 122.19, 127.52, 128.41, 130.79,
130.93, 132.99, 178.89, 201.71.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enhancement of the Reactivity of Photochemically Generated Enediynes via
Keto-Enol Tautomerization
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
