$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (Z)-Non-3-enal (3b). To a solution of
(Z)-non-3-enol (2b, 0.429 g, 3.02 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (30 mL) under argon was
added at 0°C the DMP (1.66 g, 3.91 mmol). After 5 min, the reaction
mixture was allowed to warm up to r.t. and stirred for 1 h, then cooled
down to -15°C and diluted with pentane (30 mL). The white suspension was
quickly filtered through a pad of silica gel pre-impregnated with
Et2O-pentane (1:4) and cooled between -40°C and -50°C. The silica was
rinsed with cold Et2O-pentane (100 mL, 1:4). The clear solution was
concentrated and dried by azeotropic distillation of benzene under
vacuum. The (Z)-non-3-enal (3b) was obtained. Non-3-ynal (7b). Non-3-ynol
(6b, 0.449 g, 3.21 mmol) was reacted with DMP (1.76 g, 4.15 mmol) under
the same conditions as described for the non- 3-enol and led after
working up by filtration to pure non-3-ynal (7b). Colorless oil, yield
0.425 g, 96%. Rf = 0.63 (Et2O-pentane, 1:1). IR (film): 2859, 2251, 1731,
910 cm-1. 1H NMR: δ = 9.58 (t, 1 H, J = 1.9 Hz, CHO), 3.20 (td, 2 H, J =
2.5, 1.9 Hz, CH2CHO), 2.18 (tt, 2 H, J = 7.0, 2.5 Hz, CH2CH2C), 1.54-
1.44 (m, 2 H, CH2CH2C), 1.39-1.23 [m, 4 H, (CH3CH2)2], 0.88 (t, 3 H, J =
7.6 Hz, CH3). 13C NMR: δ = 196.2 (CHO), 86.3 (CH2CH2C), 70.2 (CCH2CHO),
34.7 (CH2CHO), 31.1, 28.5, 22.3, 18.8 (4 CH2), 14.0 (CH3).
