$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM tert-Butyl 2-(tert-butoxycarbonyl-amino)-3-oxobutanoate, 15 A solution of
Dess-Martin periodinane (2.88 g, 1.2 eq.) in dichloromethane (50 mL) was
added at room temperature and under nitrogen atmosphere to a solution of
the protected amino acid 14 (1.56 g, 5.67 mmol) in dichloromethane (20
mL). The reaction mixture was stirred under those conditions for 3 h and
then diluted with dichloromethane (50 mL) before quenching with a sodium
bicarbonate saturated solution containing 0.5 M sodium sulfite (50 mL).
Phases were separated and the organic layer was washed with saturated
sodium bicarbonate (50 mL), water (50 mL), then dried over magnesium
sulfate, filtered and evaporated to give the crude which was eluted from
a pad of silica using a 7:3 hexane/ethyl acetate mixture. Evaporation of
the solvent gave tert-butyl 2-(tert-butoxycarbonyl-amino)-3-oxobutanoate
15. Yield 1.44 g, 93%, colorless oil. TLC: 7:3 hexane/EtOAc, Rf = 0.30.
IR (neat) ν/cm-1: 1750 (OC=O), 1719 (OC=O). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
5.66 (bs, 1H), 4.90 (d, J = 7.0, 1H), 2.34 (bs, 3H), 1.47 (s, 9H), 1.43
(s, 9H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 199.5, 165.2, 154.8, 83.6, 80.2,
64.9, 28.2, 27.7. HR ESI-MS: 296.1470 ([M+Na]+, C13H23NNaO5+, calc.
296.1468).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Dess-Martin oxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
