$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of this anilide-alcohol (1.43g,
4.48 mmol) in DMSO (15 mL) was added IBX (2.51 g, 8.95 mmol) and the
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 12 h. The reaction
mixture was quenched upon addition of 5% aqueous NaHCO3 (50 mL) and
diluted with EtOAc (50 mL). The layers were separated and the organic
layer was washed with 5% aqueous NaHCO3 (2 x 20 mL), water (2 x 20 mL)
and brine (30 mL) and then dired (Na2SO4) and concentrated.
