$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (Z)-Non-3-enal (3b). To a solution of
(Z)-non-3-enol (2b, 0.429 g, 3.02 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (30 mL) under argon was
added at 0°C the DMP (1.66 g, 3.91 mmol). After 5 min, the reaction
mixture was allowed to warm up to r.t. and stirred for 1 h, then cooled
down to -15°C and diluted with pentane (30 mL). The white suspension was
quickly filtered through a pad of silica gel pre-impregnated with
Et2O-pentane (1:4) and cooled between -40°C and -50°C. The silica was
rinsed with cold Et2O-pentane (100 mL, 1:4). The clear solution was
concentrated and dried by azeotropic distillation of benzene under
vacuum. The (Z)-non-3-enal (3b) was obtained. Hex-3-ynal (7a). Hex-3-ynol
(6a, 0.313 g, 3.19 mmol) was reacted with DMP (1.75 g, 4.13 mmol) under
the same conditions as described for the non-3-enol and led after working
up to pure hex-3-ynal (7a). Yield 0.29 g, 95%. IR (film): 2852, 2250,
1729, 908 cm-1. 1H NMR: δ = 9.48 (t, 1 H, J = 1.9 Hz, CHO), 3.10 (td, 2
H, J = 2.5, 1.9 Hz, CH2CHO), 2.11 (qt, 2 H, J = 7.6, 2.5 Hz, CH3CH2),
1.03 (t, 3 H, J = 7.6 Hz, CH3). 13C NMR: δ = 196.2 (CHO), 87.5 (CH3CH2C),
69.6 (CCH2CHO), 34.6 (CH2CHO), 20.7 (CH3CH2), 14.0 (CH3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Clean and efficient oxidation of homoallylic and homopropargylic alcohols
to β,γ-unsaturated aldehydes by the Dess-Martin periodinane
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wavrin, Laurence; Viala, Jacques
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2002), (3), 326-330

