$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Oxidation of 3,4-dimethoxybenzyl alcohol (7a)
and dimer model compound (1) on 10 g and 5 g scale: To a 1 L
round-bottom, three-necked flask equipped with a stir bar was added
veratryl alcohol (59.4 mmol, 10 g) or dimeric model compound 1 (15 mmol,
5.1 g), 5 mol % of 4-acetamido-TEMPO, 200 mL acetonitrile and 6 mL water.
The flask was equipped with a condenser and sealed with rubber septum.
Oxygen gas was bubbled through the solution for ca. 10 minutes. Then, 10
mol% of nitric acid (67%) and 10 mol% of hydrochloric acid (37%) were
injected through the septum. In addition, four balloons of oxygen
attached to a syringe needle were attached to the top of septa. The
reaction mixture was stirred at 45 °C and monitored by TLC. These
reactions took 3 h and 9 h for 7a and 1, respectively. The solvent was
evaporated and the residue was washed with aqueous solution of NaHCO3 (10
%) and was extracted with ethyl acetate. The organic layers were
combined, dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated under vacuum. The
residue was subjected to column chromatography to obtain the
corresponding carbonyl compound in 94% and 96% isolated yield of 8a and
3, respectively. 3,4-Dimethoxy-benzaldehyde (8a): Chromatography solvent:
hexanes:ethyl acetate (8:1). Spectral data are consistent with those
reported in the literature.12
1-(3,4-Dimethoxyphenyl)-3-hydroxy-2-(2-methoxyphenoxy)-1-propanone (3):
Chromatography solvent: hexanes:ethyl acetate (2:1). Spectral data are
consistent with those reported in the literature.2 Yield 96%. Spectral
data are consistent with those reported in the literature.2 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.74 (dd, J = 8.2, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 7.62 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H),
7.01-6.83 (m, 5H), 5.39 (t, J = 5.6 Hz, 1H), 4.07 (t, J = 5.6, 2H), 3.95
(s, 3H), 3.92 (s, 3H), 3.86 (s, 3H), 2.97 (b s, 1H). HRMS (EI) calculated
for C18H20O6Na [M + Na]+ 355.1158, found 355.1153.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, optimized on oxidation agent, optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Chemoselective Metal-Free Aerobic Alcohol Oxidation in Lignin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Rahimi, Alireza; Azarpira, Ali; Kim, Hoon; Ralph, John; Stahl, Shannon S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2013), 135(17), 6415-6418

