$DATUM Oxidation Reactions of 9.
(5α,6β,11α,16β,21α)-1,7,12,17,22-Pentaoxapentaspiro[4.0.4.0.4.0.4.0.4.1]hexacosan-26-one
(22). A. Oxidation with PDC. To a solution of 19 (34.6 mg, 0.09 mmol) in
CH2Cl2 (15 mL) was added pyridinium dichromate (320 mg, 0.85 mmol) and
powdered 3 A molecular sieves (1 g). The mixture was stirred for 24 h,
diluted with ether, and filtered through a pad of silica gel. The
filtrate was concentrated. 32.4 mg (94%) of 22 as a white solid. mp 115
°C; IR (CHCl3, cm-1) 1720; 1H NMR (300 MHz, C6D6) δ 4.06-3.99 (m, 2 H),
3.79-3.69 (m, 4 H), 3.65-3.53 (m, 4 H), 2.54-2.37 (m, 6 H), 2.16-1.94 (m,
6 H), 1.71-1.46 (m, 8 H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, C6D6) ppm 93.3, 90.5, 90.0,
69.1, 68.1, 67.5, 32.9, 30.9, 30.8, 30.6, 29.2, 28.9, 26.2; MS m/z (M+)
calcd 378.2042, obsd 378.2027. Anal. Calcd for C21H30O6: C, 66.64; H,
7.99. Found: C, 66.66; H, 8.04.
