$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of the above allylic alcohol (5.560 g, 6.47 mmol) in CH2Cl2
(60 mL) at 0 °C was added Dess-Martin periodinane (4.15 g, 9.78 mmol).
After being stirred at room temperature for 1 h, the reaction was
quenched with sat. NaHCO3 aq. and sat. Na2S2O3 aq. The resultant mixture
was diluted with ether, the organic layer was separated, washed with
brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The residue was purified by silica gel column chromatography
(hexanes / ethyl acetate = 8/1 to 6/1) to afford diene 10 (5.235 g, 6.107
mmol, 94%) as a colorless amorphous. Rf = 0.27 (hexane/ethyl acetate =
3/1); IR (film) 3064, 3030, 2933, 2860, 1871, 1738, 1699, 1612, 1587,
1514, 1496, 1471, 1402, 1363, 1302, 1250, 1173, 1092, 827, 768, 737, 698,
654 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.17–7.34 (12H, m), 6.86 (1H, d, J =
8.5 Hz), 6.84 (1H, d, J = 8.5 Hz), 6.63 (0.5H, dd, J = 17.0, 10.5 Hz),
6.59 (0.5H, dd, J = 17.0, 10.5 Hz), 6.36 (0.5H, dd, J = 17.0, 1.5 Hz),
6.26 (0.5H, dd, J = 17.0, 1.5 Hz), 5.77-5.87 (1.5H, m), 5.62 (0.5H, dd, J
= 10.5, 1.5 Hz), 5.34 (0.5H, ddd, J = 17.5, 1.5, 1.5 Hz), 5.31 (0.5H,
ddd, J = 17.5, 1.5, 1.5 Hz), 5.22 (0.5H, d, J = 10.5 Hz), 5.19 (0.5H, d,
J = 10.5 Hz), 4.30-4.60 (6H, m), 4.23 (0.5H, dd, J = 8.0, 4.5 Hz),
4.08-4.19 (1.5H, m), 3.62-3.80 (6H, m), 3.50-3.59 (2H, m), 2.97-3.39 (6H,
m), 2.62 (1H, m), 2.56 (0.5H, ddd, J = 12.0, 4.5, 4.5 Hz), 2.34 (0.5H,
ddd, J = 12.0, 4.5, 4.5 Hz), 2.08-2.24 (2H, m), 1.78 (0.5H, m), 1.55-1.70
(1.5H, m), 1.30-1.50 (2H, m), 1.01 (4.5H, s), 0.99 (4.5H, s), 0.97 (4.5H,
s), 0.95 (4.5H, s); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 200.7, 199.3, 159.3,
138.6, 138.4, 138.1, 138.0, 135.4, 135.3, 132.0, 131.9, 130.1, 130.0,
129.7, 129.3, 128.7, 128.4X2, 128.3X2, 127.9, 127.8X2, 127.7X2, 127.6,
127.5, 127.4, 118.4, 118.3, 113.8X2, 81.2, 81.0, 80.9, 78.8, 78.6, 77.6,
77.4, 76.6, 76.2X2, 76.0, 75.9X2, 75.8, 75.5, 72.9, 72.8, 72.2, 72.1,
71.0, 70.9, 70.4, 67.0X2, 66.8, 55.3, 39.8, 38.8, 35.7, 35.2, 35.0, 32.2,
32.0, 27.4X2, 27.0, 22.6, 19.9X2; ESI-MS m/z 874 [(M+NH4)+]; Anal. calcd
for C50H68O10Si: C, 70.06; H, 8.00. Found: C, 69.67; H, 8.0
