$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM α -ORGANOSULFONYLOXYLATION: GENERAL PROCEDURE Alcohol (5 mmol) was added
in one portion to a stirred suspension of Dess-Martin periodinane (15
mmol) and organosulfonic acid (15 mmol) in CH3CN (20mL), and the reaction
mixture was refluxed for 4 h. Solvent was removed under reduced pressure,
and the residue obtained was diluted by adding CHCl3 (60 mL) and washed
with saturated solution of NaHCO3 (2 x 35 mL) and brine (60 mL). The
organic layer was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and concentrated under
reduced pressure to give crude α -organosulfonyloxylated product. Pure
product was obtained after column chromatography (SiO2, mesh size 60-120,
eluent, ethyl acetate-hexane, 15:85).
2-(4-Nitrophenyl)-2-oxo-ethyl-4-methanebenzene-sulfonate (Entry 1),
Solid. yield 92%. Mp 130°C (lit.[8b] 130-131°C). IR (KBr): νmax = 1180,
1340, 1710 cm-1. 1H NMR (400MHz, CDCl3): δ 2.47 (s, 3 H), 5.25 (s, 2 H),
7.37 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 2 H), 7.83 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 2 H), 8.03 (d, J = 8.9
Hz, 2 H), 8.32 (d, J = 8.9 Hz, 2 H) ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM products depend on reaction conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One-Pot Protocol for Synthesis of α-Organosulfonyloxy Ketones from
Secondary Alcohols Using Hypervalent Iodine(V)-Mediated Oxidations
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Deshmukh, Swapnil S.; Huddar, Sameerana N.; Akamanchi, Krishnacharya G.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2009), 39(17), 3101-3110

