$DATUM 9-(tert-Butyldimethylsilyloxy)-5,6,13,14-tetradehydro-7,8,9,10,11,12-hexahydrobenzo[12]-annulen-7-one
(30). A solution of the 29 (a mixture of both isomers, 0.660 g, 1.864
mmol) in dry dichloromethane (10 mL) was added dropwise to a stirred
suspension of the Dess-Martin periodinane (1.160 g, 2.74 mmol) in dry
dichloromethane (30 mL). After 3 h the reaction mixture was diluted with
ether (50 mL), stirred for 30 min, and washed with 5% sodium
hydrocarbonate aqueous solution (50 mL) and brine (50 mL). Aqueous phase
was back-extracted with ether (50 mL). Combined organic phases were dried
over magnesium sulphate, filtered, and evaporated under reduced pressure.
Crude product was purified by column chromatography (5% ethyl acetate in
hexanes, Rf = 0.30) yielding 0.598 g (1.699 mmol, 91%) of 30 as
colourless viscous oil. FW calc. for C22H28O2Si: 352.1859, EI-HRMS found:
352.1864, EI-MS m/z: 337(1) [M+ -CH3], 295(100) [M+ -57 (t-Bu)], 280(6),
267(10), 253(13), 235(8), 221(14), 203(7), 193(7), 191(7), 178(19),
165(21), 152(9), 138(9), 129(3), 115(3), 112(3), 104(2); 1H-NMR (300
MHz): 0.08 (two singlets 3.9 Hz apart, 6H), 0.88 (s, 9H), 1.65-1.92 (m,
3H), 2.19-2.31 (m, 1H), 2.45-2.55 (ddd, J1 = 17.7 Hz, J2 = 9.9 Hz, J3 =
3.6 Hz, 1H), 2.62-2.71 (m, 2H), 2.91 (dd, J1 = 13.8 Hz, J2 = 7.2 Hz, 1H),
4.75 (tt, J1 = 6.9 Hz, J2 = 5.4 Hz, 1H), 7.26-7.31 (m, 1H), 7.35-7.44 (m,
2H), 7.54-7.57 (m, 1H); 13C-NMR (75 MHz): -4.62, -4.37, 17.98, 19.03,
22.99, 25.75, 36.40, 53.25, 68.76, 80.10, 90.91, 91.86, 96.31, 123.13,
127.59, 128.96, 130.66, 130.93, 133.19, 186.12.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
