$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: IV. General procedure for oxidation of lignin
model compounds (7a-i): To a 25 mL high pressure tube with a stir bar was
added the lignin model compound (1 mmol) and 5 mol % of 4-acetamido-TEMPO
(0.05 mmol, 10.6 mg). The tube was sealed, evacuated and filled to 1.1
atm with oxygen gas. Then, 9.4 μL of nitric acid (67%) (0.1 mmol, 6.3 mg)
in 1 mL acetonitrile and 9.9 μL of hydrochloric acid (37%) (0.1 mmol,
3.65 mg) in 1 mL of acetonitrile were injected through the septum. An
additional 3 mL of acetonitrile and 260 μL of water were injected. The
reaction mixture was stirred for 24 h at 45 °C. The solvent was
evaporated and the residue was subjected to column chromatography to
obtain the corresponding carbonyl compound.
2-Methoxy-1,2-diphenyl-ethanone (8b): Chromatography solvent:
hexanes:ethyl acetate (10:1). Spectral data are consistent with those
reported in the literature.13
1-(4-Hydroxy-3,5-dimethoxyphenyl)-3-hydroxy-2-(2-methoxyphenoxy)-1-propanone
(8i): Chromatography solvent: hexanes:ethyl acetate (1:1). Spectral data
are consistent with those reported in the literature.16 Yield 91%. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.42 (s, 2H), 7.02-6.86 (m, 4H),.02 (s, 1H), 5.39 (t,
J = 4.6 Hz, 1H), 4.11 (d, J = 4.6 Hz, 2H), 3.85 (s, 6H), 3.83 (s, 3H),
3.08 (b s, 1H). HRMS (ESI) calculated for C18H20O7Na [M + Na]+ 371.1107,
found 371.1103.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Chemoselective Metal-Free Aerobic Alcohol Oxidation in Lignin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Rahimi, Alireza; Azarpira, Ali; Kim, Hoon; Ralph, John; Stahl, Shannon S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2013), 135(17), 6415-6418

