$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 4-formylcubane-1-carboxylate (27). Dess-Martin periodinane (1.43
g, 3.38 mmol) was added portionwise to methyl
4-(hydroxymethyl)cubane-1-carboxylate (0.59 g, 3.07 mmol) in DCM (29 mL)
at room temperature. The resulting solution was stirred at room
temperature for 30 minutes. The reaction mixture was diluted with Et2O
(20 mL) and poured into saturated NaHCO3 (20 mL) containing sodium
thiosulfate (3.4 g, 21.5 mmol). The resulting suspension was stirred
vigourously for 10 minutes, before separating the layers. The organic
layer was washed with water (20 mL), dried (Na2SO4), filtered and
evaporated to afford crude product. The crude product was purified by
flash silica chromatography (elution gradient 0 to 50% EtOAc in heptane).
Pure fractions were evaporated to dryness. Yield: (0.525 g, 90 %) as a
colourless solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, 27 °C) δ 9.75 (s, 1H),
4.41-4.33 (m, 3H), 4.30-4.23 (m, 3H), 3.72 (s, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Cubanes in Medicinal Chemistry: Synthesis of Functionalized Building
Blocks
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wlochal, Joanna; Davies, Robert D. M.; Burton, Jonathan
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(16), 4094-4097

