$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedures for the Preparation of
1,5-onctadien-7-yn-4-ones 7 General Procedure G. To a stirred suspension
of Dess-Martin periodinane (6.50 mmol) in dichloromethane (20 ml) and
pyridine (13.0 mmol) was added 6 (3.25 mmol) at 0 °C. The reaction
mixture was warmed up to room temperature and stirred for 30 min. The
mixture was then diluted with Et2O and passed through Celite. The
residual solid was washed with Et2O thoroughly. The filtrate was
concentrated under reduced pressure and purified by silica gel flash
column chromatography to give 7.
(E)-6-Benzyloxymethyl-3-methyl-8-phenyl-1,5-octadien-7-yn-4-one (7n);
Following the General Procedure G; purified by silica gel column
chromatography (hexane/EtOAc = 5/1) (89% yield, yellow oil). 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 1.27 (d, J= 6.8 Hz, 3H), 3.56 (quint, J= 6.8 Hz, 1H), 4.24 (d,
J= 1.7 Hz, 2H), 4.62 (s, 2H), 5.17 (dt, J= 10.3, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 5.20 (dt,
J= 17.4, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 5.91 (ddd, J= 17.6, 10.2, 7.8 Hz, 1H), 6.77 (t, J=
1.7 Hz, 1H), 7.30-7.38 (m, 8H), 7.51-7.56 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ
15.78, 50.85, 72.23, 72.77, 86.46, 100.77, 116.92, 122.36, 127.73,
127.93, 128.38, 128.52, 128.82, 129.29, 132.21, 133.31, 137.43, 137.52,
198.84; HRMS (FAB) calcd for C23H23O2 (M++H) 331.1698, found 331.1684.
