$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To (COCl)2 (33 g, 0.26 mol) in 300 mL CH2Cl2 at -78 °C was added a
solution of DMSO (41.4 g, 0.53 mol) in 100 mL CH2Cl2 through cannula. The
reaction was stirred at -78 °C for 1 h, to which a solution of alcohol 1a
(30.5 g, 0.26 mol) in 100 mL CH2Cl2 was added through cannula. The
reaction was stirred at -78 °C for additional 30 min, and Et3N (184 mL,
1.31 mol) was added slowly. The resulting white slurry was stirred at 0
°C for 30 min, followed by 25°C for 1 h, at which time 400 mL of 3 M
aqueous HCl was added. The organic phase was washed with 400 mL saturated
aqueous NaHCO3, dried over Na2SO4, and carefully concentrated in vacuo.
The residue was distilled at reduced pressure (65 °C, 20 mbar) to provide
aldehyde 2 (26.4 g, 0.23 mol) as a colorless oil in 89% yield. 2, yield
(26.4 g, 0.23 mol, 89%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 9.60 (s, 1H), 2.16
(s, 3H), 1.33 (s, 6H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Swern oxidn.
