$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM IV. General procedure for oxidation of lignin model compounds (7a-i): To
a 25 mL high pressure tube with a stir bar was added the lignin model
compound (1 mmol) and 5 mol % of 4-acetamido-TEMPO (0.05 mmol, 10.6 mg).
The tube was sealed, evacuated and filled to 1.1 atm with oxygen gas.
Then, 9.4 μL of nitric acid (67%) (0.1 mmol, 6.3 mg) in 1 mL acetonitrile
and 9.9 μL of hydrochloric acid (37%) (0.1 mmol, 3.65 mg) in 1 mL of
acetonitrile were injected through the septum. An additional 3 mL of
acetonitrile and 260 μL of water were injected. The reaction mixture was
stirred for 24 h at 45 °C. The solvent was evaporated and the residue was
subjected to column chromatography to obtain the corresponding carbonyl
compound. 2-Methoxy-1,2-diphenyl-ethanone (8b): Chromatography solvent:
hexanes:ethyl acetate (10:1). Spectral data are consistent with those
reported in the literature.13 Yield 87%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
8.00-7.98 (m, 2H), 7.52-7.45 (m, 3H), 7.41-2.27 (m, 3H), 5.52 (s, 1H),
3.46 (s, 3H). HRMS (EI) calculated for C15H15O2 [M + H]+ 227.1072, found
227.1075.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Chemoselective Metal-Free Aerobic Alcohol Oxidation in Lignin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Rahimi, Alireza; Azarpira, Ali; Kim, Hoon; Ralph, John; Stahl, Shannon S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
