$DATUM The alcohol mixture (183 mg, 0.48 mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (25 mL),
treated with the Dess-Martin periodinane (351 mg, 0.96 mmol), stirred for
48 h, and concentrated in vacuo. Chromatography of the residue on silica
gel (elution with 50% ethyl acetate in petroleum ether containing 1 %
triethylamine), followed by recrystallization from ethyl acetate gave 168
mg (86%) of 35 as white crystals.
(5α,6β,11β,16β,21α)-1,7,12,17,22-Pentaoxapentaspiro[4.0.4.0.4.0.4.0.4.1]
hexacosan-26-one (35). mp 144-146 °C; IR (CHCl3, cm-1) 1713, 1063; 1H NMR
