$DATUM (S)-4-tert-butyl-2-(tert-butoxycarbonylamino)-4-oxobutanoate (5) To a
solution of alcohol 11 (0.284 g, 1.03 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (5 mL), solid
NaHCO3 (0.861 g, 10.25 mmol) and Dess-Martin periodinane reagent (5.1 mL
0.3 M CH2Cl2 solution, 1.53 mmol) was added. The solution was stirred at
room temperature for 1 h. Sodium thiosulfate solution (1.0 M, 5 mL) was
added and the resulting biphasic mixture was vigorously stirred for 5 min
and saturated NaHCO3 (5 mL) was then added. The mixture was then
extracted with CH2Cl2 (15 mL × 3). The combined organic layers were dried
over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo to afford crude product.
Flash chromatography (EtOAc/Hexanes, 20/80, V/V) furnished aldehyde 5
(0.243 g, 86%) as a white crystalline solid.
(S)-4-tert-butyl-2-(tert-butoxycarbonylamino)-4-oxobutanoate (5), yield
(0.243 g, 86%). mp 61.5 - 63 °C (lit.1 60 - 62 °C; lit.2 66 - 67 °C);
[α]23.5 D = + 18.6 (c = 1.95, CH2Cl2) and [α]25 D = -26.1 (c = 1.5,
absolute EtOH) [lit1 [α]21 D = + 20.7 (c = 1.95, CH2Cl2); lit3 [α]25 D =
-21.6 (c = 1.5, EtOH)]; 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.73 (s, 1 H), 5.35 (d,
1 H, J = 6 Hz), 4.47 (m, 1 H), 2.97 (t, 2 H, J = 4.4 Hz), 1.45 (s, 9 H),
1.44 (s, 9 H); 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3) δ 199.4, 170.1, 155.5, 82.8, 80.2,
49.6, 46.5, 28.4, 28.0; HRMS calcd for C13H23NaNO5 (M + Na)+: 296.1474,
found: 286.1469.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM literature preparation, Dess-Martin oxidation
