$DATUM 6-[2-(Trimethylsilylethynyl)phenyl]hex-5-ynal (23). A solution of 22
(3.139 g, 11.63 mmol) in (3.139 g, 11.63 mmol) in dry dichloromethane (5
mL) was added dropwise to a stirred suspension of the Dess-Martin
periodinane (6.410 g, 15.12 mmol, 1.3 equiv.) in dry dichloromethane (50
mL). After stirring for 2.5 hours at room temperature, the reaction
mixture was diluted with ether (200 mL), and stirred for another 30 min.
The solution was washed with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution (50 mL),
brine (50 mL), dried with MgSO4, and evaporated under reduced pressure.
Crude product was purified by column chromatography (6% Ethyl acetate in
Hexanes, Rf = 0.15) to yield 2.643 g (9.86 mmol, 85 %) of aldehyde 23. FW
calc. for C17H20OSi: 268.1283, EI-HRMS found: 268.1289, EI-MS m/z: 268
[M+], 267(12) [M+-1], 253(100), 237(14), 235(14), 225(29), 209(12),
197(15), 195(22), 178(43), 165(32), 152(33), 139(7), 129(11), 115(5),
104(3), 97(4), 89(5), 75(51), 73(92), 59(65), 53(18), 45(25); 1H-NMR (300
MHz): 0.26 (s, 9H), 1.96 (qin, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 2.56 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 2H),
2.70 (m, 2H), 7.17-7.26 (m, 2H), 7.35-7.41 (m, 1H), 7.42-7.47 (m, 1H),
9.84 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (75 MHz), 0.02, 19.01, 21.20, 42.83, 80.33, 90.33,
97.95, 103.79, 125.46, 126.37, 127.36, 128.14, 131.80, 132.26, 201.65.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enhancement of the Reactivity of Photochemically Generated Enediynes via
Keto-Enol Tautomerization
