$DATUM Procedures for the Preparation of 1,5-onctadien-7-yn-4-ones 7 General
Procedure G. To a stirred suspension of Dess-Martin periodinane (6.50
mmol) in dichloromethane (20 ml) and pyridine (13.0 mmol) was added 6
(3.25 mmol) at 0 °C. The reaction mixture was warmed up to room
temperature and stirred for 30 min. The mixture was then diluted with
Et2O and passed through Celite. The residual solid was washed with Et2O
thoroughly. The filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure and
purified by silica gel flash column chromatography to give 7.
1-((Z)-2-Phenylethynyl-1-cyclooctenyl)-3-buten-1-one (7a); Following the
General Procedure G; purified by silica gel column chromatography
(hexane/EtOAc = 10/1) (82% yield, pale yellow oil). 1H NMR (CDCl3 ) δ
1.48-1.55 (m, 4H), 1.63-1.68 (m, 2H), 1.75-1.79 (m, 2H), 2.48-2.51 (m,
2H), 2.57-2.60 (m, 2H), 3.84 (dt, J= 7.1, 1.2 Hz, 2H), 5.14 (dq, J= 17.2,
1.5 Hz, 1H), 5.17 (dq, J= 9.8, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 6.05 (ddt, J = 17.3, 10.2,
6.8 Hz, 1H), 7.26-7.36 (m, 3H), 7.42-7.45 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ
26.18, 26.38, 28.45, 28.96, 30.30, 34.39, 47.19, 90.19, 97.42, 118.12,
122.92, 128.40, 128.56, 128.68, 131.38, 131.57, 146.61, 202.56; HRMS
(FAB) calcd for C20H23O (M++H) 279.1749, found 279.1739.
