$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: JTP-4-71: A 250 mL round bottom flask fitted
with an addition funnel was charged with nitroxide 9 (4.125 g, 18.06
mmol) and sodium bicarbonate (23.45 g, 279.1 mmol), evacuated, charged
with nitrogen, and cooled in an ice water bath. A solution of Dess-Martin
periodinane in DCM (9.243 g, 21.79 mmol in 85 mL) was added dropwise over
36 minutes and the resulting orange mixture was stirred at rt for 1 h
over which time the color became yellow, once the color began to darken;
work up was started. Transfer reaction mixture to separatory funnel with
diethyl ether (200 mL) causing a white precipitation, presumably
iodo-compounds, wash with 1.5 M aq. NaOH (3 × 150 mL) and brine (2 × 100
mL). Drying over magnesium sulfate and evaporation in rotary evaporator
gave a brown crude oil which was purified by column chromatography
(silica gel, hexanes/ethyl acetate, 5:2) to give a dark yellow oil which
was transferred to a vial with EtOAc and mostly evaporated with a stream
of nitrogen to give an orange solution which was cooled in an acetone/
dry ice bath. Removal of solvents and washing with pentane gave nitroxide
10 as yellow crystals (0.939 g), the remaining solvent was evaporated to
give a yellow solid (1.674 g, 64% overall). Yield 1.313g, 82%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Dess-Martin oxidation, dropwise addition of DMP/DCM
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Reduction Kinetics of Sterically Shielded Pyrrolidine
Nitroxides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
