$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of COOMe-HNE (15). Dess-Martin periodinane (1.4 g, 3.4 mmol)
was added to a solution of 14 (1.0 g, 2.8 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (14 mL). After
1 h, the reaction mixture was concentrated and purified by column
chromatography (10 to 20% EtOAc/hexanes) yielding the product (0.80 g,
81%) as a colorless liquid. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 9.53 (d, 1H, J = 8.0 Hz),
6.76 (dd, 1H, J = 4.5, 15.5 Hz), 6.21 (ddd, 1H, J = 1.5, 8.0, 15.5 Hz),
4.36 (m, 1H), 3.62 (s, 3H), 2.26 (t, 2H, J = 7.4 Hz), 1.60-1.52 (m, 4H),
1.30-1.20 (m, 8H), 0.87 (s, 9H), 0.02 (s, 3H), -0.01 (s, 3H); 13C NMR
(CDCl3) δ 193.6, 174.2, 160.2, 130.6, 71.5, 51.4, 37.0, 34.0, 29.3, 29.0,
28.9, 25.7, 24.8, 24.7, 18.1, -4.7, -5.0; HRMS (ESI) calculated 379.2275
(M + Na), observed 379.2287.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Dess-Martin oxidation
