$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedures for the Preparation of Aldehydes 11m-p General Procedure D. To
a stirred suspension of Dess-Martin periodinane (11.2 mmol) in
dichloromethane (20 ml) and pyridine (22.4 mmol) was added 14 (5.6 mmol)
at 0 °C. The reaction mixture was warmed to room temperature and stirred
for 30 min. The mixture was then diluted with Et2O and passed through
Celite. The residual solid was washed with Et2O thoroughly. The filtrate
was concentrated under reduced pressure. Purification by silica gel flash
column chromatography gave 11.
(E)-3-Benzyloxymethyl-5-phenyl-2-penten-4-ynal (11m); Following the
General Procedure D; purified by silica gel column chromatography
(hexane/EtOAc = 5/1) (E/Z = 9/1 mixture: 80% yield, yellow oil). The
single isomer was obtained by gel permeation chromatography;. 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 4.30 (d, J = 1.9 Hz, 2H), 4.64 (s, 2H), 6.57 (dt, J = 8.3, 1.9
Hz, 1H), 7.30-7.44 (m, 8H), 7.48-7.52 (m, 2H), 10.26 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 1H);
13C NMR (CDCl3 ) δ 71.29, 72.91, 82.93, 101.25, 121.39, 127.68, 127.98,
128.52, 128.56, 129.75, 131.92, 132.27, 132.29, 137.22, 143.02, 192.26;
HRMS (FAB) calcd for C19H17O2 (M++H) 277.1229, found 277.1237.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, Dess-Martin oxidation, stereoisomers separated by gel
permeation chromatography
