$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: III. Typical experimental procedure for
IBX-mediated oxidative rearrangement. To a stirred solution of tertially
allylic alcohol (1a) (100 mg, 574 μmol) in DMSO (3 ml)was added IBX1 (320
mg, 1.15 mmol) at room temperature. After IBX was dissolved, thereaction
was warmed to 55 °C and stirred for 1 h. After cooling to rt, water was
added andthe mixture was extracted with diethyl ether. The organic
extract was washed with brine,dried (MgSO4), and concentrated. The
residue was purified by silica gel columnchromatography (EtOAc-hexane = 1
: 4) 5-Methyltricyclo[5.2.1.02,6]deca-4,8-dien-3-one (10b), yield 79%. IR
(neat): 1695 cm-1; 1H-NMR δ 5.98 (dd, 1H, J= 5.6, 3.0 Hz),5.79 (dd, 1H,
J= 5.6, 2.9 Hz), 5.69 (s, 1H), 3.22 (t, 1H, J= 4.9Hz), 3.18 (s, 1H), 3.01
(s, 1H), 2.85 (t, 1H, J= 5.1 Hz), 1.98(s,3H), 1.77 (d, 1H, J= 8.3 Hz),
1.59 (d, 1H, J= 8.7 Hz); 13C-NMR(100MHz, CDCl3) δ 209.8, 178.06, 133.4,
132.9, 131.4, 52.4,51.7, 51.1, 44.3, 43.3, 18.2; MS m/z 160 (M+), 66
(100%); HRMSCalcd. C11H12O: 160.0888. Found: 160.0877.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry (- reagent)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Oxidative Rearrangement of Cyclic Tertiary Allylic Alcohols with IBX in
DMSO
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
