$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1-((Z)-2-Phenylethynyl-1-cyclooctenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (6a); Following the
General Procedure E; General Procedure E. To a stirred solution of 11
(4.50 mmol) in Et2O (25 ml) was added allyl Grignard reagent (0.81 M
solution in Et2O, 9.00 mmol) at 0 °C and stirred for 30 min. The mixture
was then quenched by addition of saturated aq. NH4Cl, extracted with
EtOAc three times, and washed with brine. The organic layers were dried
over Na2SO4 and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by silica gel column chromatography to give 6.
(Z)-6-(5-Chloropent-1-ynyl)-10-methyl-1,5,9-undecatrien-4-one (7q);
Following the General Procedure G; purified by silica gel column
chromatography (hexane/EtOAc = 20/1) (78% yield, pale yellow oil). 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 1.62 (s, 3H), 1.69 (s, 3H), 2.06 (quint, J= 6.7 Hz, 2H), 2.26
(d, J= 3.1 Hz, 4H), 2.67 (t, J= 7.0 Hz, 2H), 3.42 (dt, J= 7.0 Hz, 2H),
3.73 (t, J= 6.1 Hz, 2H), 5.05-5.10 (m, 1H), 5.14 (dq, J= 17.1, 1.5 Hz,
1H), 5.18 (dq, J= 10.4, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 5.96 (ddt, J= 17.1, 10.4, 7.0 Hz,
1H), 6.23 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 17.35, 17.68, 25.61, 25.61, 26.69,
30.97, 39.75, 43.54, 47.44, 80.78, 101.28, 118.44, 122.44, 131.01,
131.56, 132.92, 137.38, 196.76; HRMS (FAB) calcd for C17H24ClO (M++H)
279.1516, found 279.1509.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, Dess-Martin oxidation
