$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of (biphenyl-2-yloxy)acetaldehyde
derivatives: As a representative example, the synthesis of
(3',4'-difluoro-biphenyl-2-yloxy)acetaldehyde is reported. To 100 mg of
(3',4'-difluoro-biphenyl-2-yloxy)ethanol (0.400 mmol) dissolved in CH2Cl2
(3 mL) was added Dess-Martin periodinane (212 mg, 0.500 mmol). After
stirring for 1 h at rt, the resulting mixture was diluted with CH2Cl2 (50
mL) and washed with water three times. The organic layer was collected
and dried over Na2SO4 followed by filtration and evaporation under
reduced pressure. To the resulting residue was added ether (10 mL) and
the resulting mixture was filtered to remove a white solid. The solution
was concentrated and the residue was purified by preparative TLC (CH2Cl2)
to give the desired aldehyde (77 mg, 78%).
(3',4'-difluoro-biphenyl-2-yloxy)acetaldehyde 1H-NMR (400 MHz): δ 10.79
(s, 1), 7.45-7.38 (m, 1), 7.36-7.17 (m, 4), 7.11 (dt, 1, J = 1.2, 7.6),
6.83 (dd, 1, J = 0.8, 4.4), 4.58 (s, 2). HRMS (EI+) m/z: 248.0649 (M+
C14H10F2O2 requires 248.0649).
